## What the product does now, by id (one line each)
- Capture: screen + camera + mic + tab/system audio armed together at one epoch; instant start; chips toggle any input mid-take (a real stop and a new segment); pause/resume exist in the engine with no UI (F6); every stop drains every file (P0-tail); a stop past its 5 s budget keeps what reached disk (H5); a device that dies or never delivers is said live and stamped in Recording.lost (H4); an encoder/worker/recorder death closes the segment and opens the next, ≤4 per channel (H1); the disk guard reads real storage growth and auto-stops before the disk fills (B5); the first VideoEncoder per launch is warmed at mount so a take killed at 2 s keeps ~1 s of picture after the first page load (H6).
- Elastic: sub-max takes step RATE down before loss and back up, predicted from four signals in the compositor worker (E1); max never steps and opens no composite (2 encoders); M1 will arm max's emergency floor behind a flag; ruling 09-02: bias UP (E2 retunes).
- Sync: audio anchored by a min-filter over batch arrivals minus the platform's reported latency (always 10 ms — B7); video anchored at frame READ; composite origin carried signed so the copied picture is no longer late (B9); wall-clock hold symmetric on the audio a user hears; 987 ms oracle grid (G5).
- Crash: a kill at any moment loses ~2 s (H2); the pending manifest lives in its own IndexedDB with strict durability plus localStorage, and an early keyframe closes the first fragment (H2b) — kills at 2.3-20.3 s all recovered.
- Wedge (Chrome's screen picker never settling on macOS): one press, instant 'stale' refusal, one reload; ladder rung 3 wedged three in a row — page has no move left; second origin inout-kappa-two is the standing per-site test; levers are Robert's (docs/SCREEN_WEDGE.md).
- Editor: framed stage (zoom drag, camera drag, frame presets), split/delete/undo zones, per-clip speed 0.5-2×, Tighten proposals from the capture-time envelope, trims, filmstrip + waveform lanes at 60 fps at any length, edit persisted, keys space/←/→; continue button says "roadmap" (F19).
- Export: three paths in order — instant packet copy (unedited; the composite at 1080p, or the raw channel when the step matches the take's geometry incl. `max` screen-only: 452 KB instant at 3024x1964) · smart cut (trims/cuts; re-encode only [cut → next keyframe]) · render (worker, 5-6× realtime, decode-bound); prerender makes the file before it is asked for (1.2 s after an edit settles; at STOP for max+camera, paced by pressure, first load shed); exports are persisted background jobs in a dock on every screen, parallel, restart-from-zero after refresh (J1 open); size panel = model + probe (probe 1.50× high on still text, B1b); certificate JSON in every file's comment tag; For-AI PDF export (AI1) in a worker.
- Audio: every path mixes the RAW channels; p90 makeup bounded by the p20 floor and the peak licence, u/(1+u) limiter; R128 built and inert until attenuation is allowed; capture-time envelope skips the probe; tab audio raw on every wedge rung.
- Store: OPFS blobs + IndexedDB (`inout` frozen at v2; jobs and the pending manifest in their own DBs); recovery salvages on boot and opens the take; scratch exports stream to disk (4 MB held).
- Report card (S1): ten dimensions graded at stop, `__inoutReport()` family, 60-take verdict ring; console only (Robert: bug data is not shown to users).
- Platform: capability × OS gating; Chromium verified; Safari records via MediaRecorder lanes (mic loss P8 blocked on an artifact); iOS cannot screen-record in any browser; cloud UI absent on prod (Supabase env unset); analytics noop in prod; PWA precaches the whole build (a tab across a deploy can record).

